    "ebola": {
      "sequence": "GAAIGLAWIPYFGPAAEGI",
      "description": "Core sequence of the Ebola virus GP2 internal fusion loop (residues 524-542 of Zaire ebolavirus GP). This 19-residue peptide (GAAIGLAWIPYFGPAAEGI) is part of the complete 54-residue fusion loop (2LCZ: AQPKCNPNLHYWTTQDEGAAIGLAWIPYFGPAAEGIYIEGLMHNQDGLICGLRQ). It is 100% conserved across all six Ebola species (Zaire, Sudan, Reston, Bundibugyo, Tai Forest, and Bombali). This is a well-established target for antiviral peptides, with cyclic-minipeptides designed against this region predicted to have nanomolar affinity [citation:7][citation:12].",
